  "instructions": [
    "Heat coconut oil in a large pot over medium heat and sauté ginger, garlic, cumin, coriander, and sliced thai-bird-chili until fragrant, about 2 minutes.",
    "Add the chicken thighs, brown on all sides for 3 to 4 minutes.",
    "Pour in coconut milk, lime juice, and a splash of coconut aminos, then bring to a gentle simmer.",
    "Cover and let the chicken poach in the coconut milk until cooked through, about 20 minutes.",
    "Remove the chicken, shred it, and then stir it back into the sauce to coat with the aromatic broth.",
    "Taste and season with salt, then reduce heat to low and let the sauce thicken slightly, 5 minutes.",
    "Serve hot over steamed white rice and garnish with fresh cilantro.",
    "Enjoy the soulful blend of Jamaican and Thai flavors."
  ],
